Discussed with @ajwerner offline:

Ideally, internal executor with a not-nil txn is either planner  or collectionFactory oriented, so that the  txn is always tightly coupled with the descriptor collection.
So there’s no need for a new `ieFactory.WithTxn()` function to deal with not-nil txn without planner. Instead, we will use
``` go
func (cf *CollectionFactory) TxnWithExecutor(
	ctx context.Context,
	ief sqlutil.InternalExecutorFactory,
        sd *sessiondata.SessionData,
	db *kv.DB,
	f func(ctx context.Context, txn *kv.Txn, ie sqlutil.InternalExecutor, descriptors *Collection) error,
) error {
	ie := ief(ctx, sd)
    return cf.Txn(ctx, ie, db, func(ctx context.Context, txn *kv.Txn, descriptors *Collection) error {
    ie.SetExtraTxnState(descriptors)
    f(ctx, txn, ie, descriptors)
})
}
```
for this case.

So the existing use cases with
``` go
s.db.Txn(ctx, func(ctx context.Context, txn *kv.Txn) error{
	ie.ExecEx(...)
})
```
will be replaced with
``` go
s.collectionFactory.TxnWithExecutor(ctx, ief, s.db, sessionData, func(ctx context.Context, txn *kv.Txn, ie sqlutil.InternalExecutor, descriptors *Collection){
	ie.ExecEx(...)
})
```
